{"id":"c4c7ef5977c8925b41623ba98fcae67ecf689617","axis":"silent","repo":"datafuselabs/databend","sha":"c4c7ef5977c8925b41623ba98fcae67ecf689617","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/designs/dml-deduplication.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@","+# DML deduplication contract","+","+A deduplication label is a client retry token, not a Meta key. If a response is","+lost after a durable write commits, a retry with the same token should not","+repeat the write. Query derives the key from the authenticated execution context","+and authorized target. The marker commits atomically with the durable effect.","+","+This document distinguishes the current behavior from the target contract.","+","+## Token entry points","+","+| Entry point | Compatibility rule |","+| --- | --- |","+| SQL `SET_VAR` hint and statement `SETTINGS` clause | Keep both as statement-scoped inputs. Prefer these forms for SQL clients. |","+| HTTP `X-DATABEND-DEDUPLICATE-LABEL` | Keep it as a query-scoped input. A request header must not create a session or tenant default. |","+| SQL `SET deduplicate_label` and HTTP `session.settings` | Keep as session-scoped compatibility inputs. Clients should clear a session label after the intended write and its retries. The empty string means no label. |","+| SQL `SET GLOBAL deduplicate_label` | Reject it. Previously stored global values are ignored on load; nothing needs to be migrated. Use a statement or request token instead. |","+","+Retain existing precedence: statement settings override the query header,","+which overrides session settings. Within SQL, a `SETTINGS` clause takes","+precedence over `SET_VAR` hints when both appear. Apply the same token","+validation to all accepted forms. Do not inherit an outer label as a separate","+retry token for each nested statement in a script or procedure; a client","+retrying a whole script needs a separate contract. Explicit labels on individual","+statements follow the rules below.","+","+## Supported operations","+","+| Operation | Current behavior | Target behavior |","+| --- | --- | --- |","+| Single-target `INSERT`, `REPLACE`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`, `MERGE`, and `COPY INTO <table>` on a persistent Fuse-backed table | The interpreter can check a label before execution, and the Fuse commit path can record it. A label is currently shared across statement kinds and targets within the tenant. | Support a bounded token scoped to the authenticated principal, catalog, target, and operation kind. A retry must use the same token for the same logical operation. A successful retry may return an already-committed outcome rather than replaying the original result. |","+| Supported DML that consumes a stream but changes no table rows | A stream-offset-only commit can record a marker. | Keep this path: advancing an offset is a durable effect. A statement with no durable effect leaves no persistent marker. |","+| Supported statements inside an explicit transaction | The open transaction checks buffered labels. Only statements with persistent updates contribute markers at commit. | Keep duplicate handling local to the open transaction until commit and publish only markers tied to durable effects. Rollback leaves no persistent marker. A conflicting marker must not cause a transaction containing new work to report success. A statement token does not identify or replay the whole transaction. |","+| Temporary-table-only writes | No persistent marker is written. A label is buffered only for duplicate checks within an open transaction. | Reject a token before execution until a session-local retry contract exists. Never persist a marker for a temporary-table-only write. |","+| `COPY INTO <location>` | It consults the same lookup as table writes, but the stage sink does not record a matching marker. | Reject a token before execution until an export-specific contract exists. A table-write marker does not prove that an external file was written. |","+| Multi-table `INSERT`, other storage engines without marker support, and other statements without a retry contract | Not consistently covered; for example, multi-table `INSERT` does not pass a label to its commit plan. | Reject an explicit token on unsupported operations before execution. Do not silently run an unsupported labeled write as an ordinary write. |","+","+The supported table-write contract covers the durable commit, not all work done","+while preparing it. A concurrent retry can still do speculative work; only one","+attempt may publish the durable effect while its marker exists. Keep existing","+file-level `COPY` deduplication separate from statement retry tokens.","+","+## Compatibility and rollout","+","+- Cross-target or cross-statement-kind suppression is not a retry guarantee.","+  Some existing tests depend on this behavior (for example, reusing an","+  `INSERT` label on `REPLACE`). Update those tests when switching namespaces,","+  and keep a same-operation retry test across a reconnect.","+- Do not treat tenant-only markers as proof that a newly scoped operation","+  committed. Plan the namespace cutover with clients that have outstanding","+  labeled writes; reconcile any uncertain outcome before retrying it.","+- Continue to use normal authorization for the target even when a marker","+  exists. Do not promise exact-request matching for operations where a stable","+  request fingerprint is unavailable.","+","+## Implementation references","+","+- [Statement settings and hint resolution](../../src/query/sql/src/planner/statement_settings.rs)","+- [HTTP session settings](../../src/query/service/src/servers/http/v1/query/http_query.rs)","+  and [query label header application](../../src/query/service/src/servers/http/v1/query/http_query_context.rs)","+- [Session and global settings rules](../../src/query/settings/src/settings_global.rs)","+- [Query deduplication check](../../src/query/service/src/interpreters/common/util.rs)","+  and [Fuse table commit](../../src/query/storages/fuse/src/operations/commit.rs)","+- [Stream-offset-only commit](../../src/query/storages/fuse/src/operations/common/processors/sink_commit.rs)","+  and [existing regression](../../tests/sqllogictests/suites/ee/06_ee_stream/06_0018_stream_noop_dedup_label.test)","+- [Explicit-transaction retry test](../../tests/sqllogictests/suites/http_handler/transaction/txn_dedup_label.test)","+  and [HTTP stage-load retry test](../../tests/suites/1_stateful/07_stage_attachment/07_0002_insert_with_stage_deduplicate.sh)"],"additions":67,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/meta/api/src/api_impl/table_api.rs","lines":["@@ -1598,6 +1598,10 @@ where","         req: UpdateMultiTableMetaReq,","         txn_sender: &IdempotentKVTxnSender,","     ) -> Result<UpdateMultiTableMetaResult, KVAppError> {","+        if !req.deduplicated_labels.is_empty() && !req.has_persistent_updates() {","+            return Err(AppError::DeduplicationLabelWithoutMetaUpdate.into());","+        }","+","         let UpdateMultiTableMetaReq {","             mut update_table_metas,","             copied_files,"],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/meta/app/src/app_error.rs","lines":["@@ -948,6 +948,9 @@ pub enum AppError {","     #[error(transparent)]","     CommitTableMetaError(#[from] CommitTableMetaError),"," ","+    #[error(\"Deduplication labels require a persistent metadata update\")]","+    DeduplicationLabelWithoutMetaUpdate,","+","     #[error(transparent)]","     SharedTableSecurityPolicy(#[from] SharedTableSecurityPolicy),"," ","@@ -1482,6 +1485,9 @@ impl From<AppError> for ErrorCode {","                 ErrorCode::UndropDbWithNoDropTime(err.message())","             }","             AppError::CommitTableMetaError(err) => ErrorCode::CommitTableMetaError(err.message()),","+            AppError::DeduplicationLabelWithoutMetaUpdate => {","+                ErrorCode::InvalidArgument(app_err.to_string())","+            }","             AppError::SharedTableSecurityPolicy(err) => ErrorCode::AlterTableError(err.message()),","             AppError::InvalidMaterializedView(err) => {","                 ErrorCode::InvalidMaterializedView(err.message())"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/meta/app/src/schema/table/mod.rs","lines":["@@ -891,6 +891,16 @@ impl UpdateMultiTableMetaReq {","             && self.deduplicated_labels.is_empty()","             && self.update_temp_tables.is_empty()","     }","+","+    /// Deduplication labels and temporary table updates are not persistent work.","+    pub fn has_persistent_updates(&self) -> bool {","+        !self.update_table_metas.is_empty()","+            || !self.update_stream_metas.is_empty()","+            || self","+                .copied_files","+                .iter()","+                .any(|(_, req)| !req.file_info.is_empty())","+    }"," }"," "," /// The result of updating multiple table meta"],"additions":10,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/meta/schema-api-test-suite/src/schema_api_test_suite.rs","lines":["@@ -150,6 +150,7 @@ use databend_common_meta_app::schema::TableCloneBinding;"," use databend_common_meta_app::schema::TableCloneByGroupIdent;"," use databend_common_meta_app::schema::TableCopiedFileInfo;"," use databend_common_meta_app::schema::TableCopiedFileNameIdent;","+use databend_common_meta_app::schema::TableDeduplicationLabelIdent;"," use databend_common_meta_app::schema::TableId;"," use databend_common_meta_app::schema::TableIdHistoryIdent;"," use databend_common_meta_app::schema::TableIdList;","@@ -168,7 +169,9 @@ use databend_common_meta_app::schema::TruncateTableReq;"," use databend_common_meta_app::schema::UndropDatabaseReq;"," use databend_common_meta_app::schema::UndropTableReq;"," use databend_common_meta_app::schema::UpdateMultiTableMetaReq;","+use databend_common_meta_app::schema::UpdateStreamMetaReq;"," use databend_common_meta_app::schema::UpdateTableMetaReq;","+use databend_common_meta_app::schema::UpdateTempTableReq;"," use databend_common_meta_app::schema: